# Coding Standards

> These rules apply to **all languages and projects**. Technology-specific extensions live in the corresponding standards file — see Section 8.

---

## 1. Pre-Implementation Review (AI Responsibility)

This review is executed exclusively during the `/enrich-us` command, as part of the User Story enrichment process. The User Story must not be confirmed until all items below are resolved by the developer.

Before any spec is approved, the AI agent must review the current application state and surface all findings:

- **Conflict detection**: Identify existing code, DB structures, or business logic that may conflict with or be affected by the requested development.
- **Dependency mapping**: Detect which modules, services, models, or APIs are impacted — including non-obvious indirect dependencies.
- **Ambiguity flagging**: Surface any requirement that is unclear, incomplete, or has multiple valid interpretations. Never assume — ask.
- **Risk identification**: Flag anything that could introduce regressions, break existing behaviour, or requires cross-team coordination.
- **Open questions**: Compile a numbered list of all doubts found. Present it to the developer and wait for explicit resolution before approving the User Story.

> **Rule**: `/enrich-us` must not produce a confirmed User Story while open questions remain. If new questions arise during `develop-spec`, escalate them to the developer and pause implementation until resolved.

