## 2. SOLID Principles and Design Patterns

Apply SOLID in all object-oriented code:

- **S — Single Responsibility**: each class/function has one reason to change.
- **O — Open/Closed**: open for extension, closed for modification.
- **L — Liskov Substitution**: subtypes must be substitutable for their base types.
- **I — Interface Segregation**: clients must not depend on interfaces they don't use.
- **D — Dependency Inversion**: depend on abstractions, not concretions.

Know and apply Design Patterns when appropriate (Singleton, Factory, Facade, Dependency Injection, Observer, etc.). Reference: [refactoring.guru](https://refactoring.guru/es). Knowing when a pattern applies is enough — you do not need to memorise every implementation.

